1. Creating Custom Exceptions:
   - Checked Exception: Inherit from `java.lang.Exception`. Must be declared via `throws`
     or handled in a `try-catch` block.
   - Unchecked Exception (Standard Backend Practice): Inherit from `java.lang.RuntimeException`:
     ```java
     public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
         public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) {
             super(message);
         }
     }
     ```

2. Handling via Spring Boot Global Handler:
   - Use `@RestControllerAdvice` and `@ExceptionHandler` to intercept the custom exception
     and return an accurate HTTP status code (e.g., 404 Not Found) with a clean JSON payload:
     ```java
     @RestControllerAdvice
     public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
         @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
         public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
             return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                     .body(new ErrorResponse(404, ex.getMessage()));
         }
     }
     ```
